========================================
1. CORE CONCEPT
========================================

A roguelike "Party-Builder" using a modified standard card set. Unlike traditional card games where cards are spells you cast and forget, here your cards are your Party Members. You are the Leader (Face Card), managing a roster of adventurers, creatures, or specialists.

KEY TWIST: This is a Dual-Rank lane-based game. You deploy your cards onto a persistent board (12 slots: 5 Vanguard + 7 Rearguard). They stay and fight until they are exhausted or destroyed. Your goal is to manage this "Guild" effectively to defeat the Level 7 Superboss.

========================================
2. BASE MECHANICS
========================================

2.1 RESOURCES
-------------

HP (Leader Health)
- Reaching 0 = Death
- Protected by Vanguard units
- Starting HP by Archetype:
  * Spades: 25 HP
  * Clubs: 35 HP
  * Hearts: 30 HP
  * Diamonds: 20 HP

Deck Count (The Roster)
- Number of members in reserve
- Reaching 0 = Game Over (Party Disbanded)
- Fatigue: When deck is empty, shuffle discard → Permanently remove 1 random card from encounter

Dice (Action Points)
- Roll dice at start of turn into "Dice Pool"
- Sum = Total value to deploy units/use abilities
- Default: 2d6 (range 2-12, average 7)

2.2 CARD COSTS
--------------
- Ranks 2-10: Cost = Face Value (5♠ costs 5 dice)
- Aces: Cost = 11 dice, Stats = 11
- Diamonds: Cost = Face Value (instant spells)
- Jokers: Unique costs (see Joker section)

2.3 HAND & DRAW
---------------
- Starting Hand: 5 cards (drawn at combat start)
- Mulligan: Once per combat, shuffle any number back and redraw
- Draw Phase: Draw 1 card at start of each turn (after Turn 1)
- No hand size limit (unless modified by relics)
- No discard at end of turn (persistent hand)

2.4 TACTICAL ACTIONS (RNG Mitigation)
--------------------------------------
- Exertion: Discard 1 card → Add half its value (rounded down) to Dice Pool
- Reserve: Bank up to 2 unspent dice for next turn
- Leader Actions (Always Available):
  * Punch (1 Die): Deal 1 damage to nearest enemy
  * Guard (1 Die): Grant 1 Shield to Leader
  * Cycle (2 Dice): Discard 1 card, draw 1 card

========================================
3. CARD SYSTEM (Dual-Rank)
========================================

Every non-Diamond card has BOTH a Vanguard Effect and Rearguard Effect.

3.1 ♠️ SPADES (Strikers/Aggression)
-----------------------------------
Vanguard (Melee Striker):
- HP = Face Value
- Attack = Current HP (dynamic)
- Attacks enemy directly across

Rearguard (Ranged Attacker):
- HP = Face Value
- Attack = Fixed (2 for ranks 2-5, 4 for ranks 6-10, 6 for Ace)
- Auto-targets enemy with LOWEST current HP

3.2 ♣️ CLUBS (Defenders/Protection)
-----------------------------------
Vanguard (Tank):
- HP = Face Value × 1.5 (rounded up)
- Attack = Face Value ÷ 2 (rounded down)
- Thorns: Damage = Rank ÷ 2 (rounded down, min 1)

Rearguard (Shielder):
- HP = Face Value
- Effect: Grants Shield = Face Value ÷ 2 (rounded down) to unit directly in front each turn

3.3 ♥️ HEARTS (Menders/Vitality)
--------------------------------
Vanguard (Siphon/Paladin):
- HP = Face Value
- Attack = Face Value ÷ 2 (rounded down)
- Lifesteal: Heals self for 50% of damage dealt
- Overheal: Excess healing → Leader HP at 25% efficiency

Rearguard (Healer):
- HP = Face Value
- Effect: Heals unit directly in front for Face Value ÷ 2 (rounded down) each turn

3.4 ♦️ DIAMONDS (Spells/Abilities)
----------------------------------
- Function: Instant actions (do not occupy board slots)
- Cost: Face Value in dice
- Discarded immediately after use (unless Exhaust specified)
- Each rank (2-10) has unique spell per class (120 total spells)
- See Section 7 for complete catalog

========================================
4. BOARD & COMBAT
========================================

4.1 PLAYER BOARD (12-Slot Grid)
--------------------------------
VANGUARD (5 Slots): [V1][V2][V3][V4][V5]
- Function: Melee zone, blocks enemies, protects Rearguard
- Units here take direct enemy attacks

REARGUARD (7 Slots): [R1][R2][R3][R4][R5][R6][R7]
- Function: Support/Reserve zone
- Wider than Vanguard for support chains

SLOT ALIGNMENT:
- R2 supports V1
- R3 supports V2
- R4 supports V3 (Center)
- R5 supports V4
- R6 supports V5
- R1 (Left Flank): No direct Vanguard → Targets nearest (V1)
- R7 (Right Flank): No direct Vanguard → Targets nearest (V5)

FLANK MECHANICS:
- Support effects target nearest Vanguard unit
- Ranged attacks work normally (target lowest HP enemy)
- Harder for enemies to breach
- Less effective for direct support buffs

4.2 DEPLOYMENT RULES
--------------------
- Permanent Deployment: Cards cannot move after placement
- Replacement: Play card on occupied slot → Old unit Retired to discard (no "On Death" trigger)
- Retreat: Discard a unit to free slot without playing new card

4.3 TURN STRUCTURE
------------------
1. Start Phase: Roll dice, draw 1 card, trigger "Start of Turn" effects (Regen, Poison)
2. Deployment Phase: Play cards, use abilities, Leader actions
3. Player Combat Phase:
   a. Rearguard acts first (Support/Ranged)
   b. Vanguard attacks (Melee)
4. Enemy Combat Phase: Enemies attack left-to-right
5. End Phase: Cleanup shields (unless Plated), trigger "End of Turn" effects

4.4 COMBAT TARGETING
--------------------
Player Vanguard:
1. Attack enemy directly across (same column)
2. If empty: Attack nearest enemy (Priority: Left → Right → Backline)

Player Rearguard (Ranged):
- Auto-target lowest current HP enemy
- Unlimited range

Player Rearguard (Support):
- Target unit directly in front
- Flanks (R1/R7) target nearest Vanguard

Enemy Attacks:
1. Melee: Attack Vanguard in their column
2. Breach: If Vanguard empty → Attack Rearguard in that column
3. Leader Strike: If both rows empty → Direct Leader damage

Breach Priority (if entire Vanguard wiped):
- Center Rearguard (R3, R4, R5) first
- Inner Flanks (R2, R6)
- Outer Flanks (R1, R7)

4.5 BATTLE FATIGUE (Anti-Stall)
--------------------------------
- Starting Round 15: "The Darkness Closes In"
- All units (friendly & enemy) take 1 True Damage at end of turn
- Damage increases by +1 each subsequent turn (1, 2, 3, 4...)

========================================
5. ENEMY DESIGN
========================================

5.1 INTENT SYSTEM
-----------------
Before player acts, enemies display Intent icons:
- Sword: Attack (damage value shown)
- Shield: Buff Armor/Block
- Sparkles: Debuff/Special Ability
- Skull: Heavy/Fatal attack

5.2 ENEMY FORMATIONS
--------------------
Small Encounter (3-4 enemies):
[E1][E2][E3]
(Frontline only)

Medium Encounter (4-6 enemies):
   [S1][S2]
   Backline
[E1][E2][E3][E4]
   Frontline

Large Encounter (6-8 enemies):
  [S1][S2][S3]
    Backline
[E1][E2][E3][E4][E5]
     Frontline

Boss Encounter:
[S1][S2][S3][S4]
    Backline
[BOSS + ADDS]
   Frontline

5.3 ROTATION MECHANIC
---------------------
When Frontline enemy dies:
1. Check directly behind (same column) → Move forward
2. If none: Check left adjacent backline
3. If none: Check right adjacent backline
4. If no backline: Slot remains empty

5.4 ENEMY ARCHETYPES
--------------------
FRONTLINE:
- Brute: High HP (15), Low ATK (6) - Example: Orc Warrior
- Striker: Medium HP (8), High ATK (10) - Example: Goblin Berserker
- Elite: High HP (25), High ATK (12), Abilities - Example: Dark Knight

BACKLINE:
- Archer: Low HP (6), Medium ATK (5), Ranged - Example: Bandit Archer
- Healer: Low HP (8), No ATK, Heals 6 HP - Example: Cultist Priest
- Buffer: Low HP (7), Low ATK (2), Grants +3 ATK - Example: War Shaman
- Summoner: Medium HP (12), Low ATK (1), Summons 2/2 - Example: Necromancer

5.5 EXAMPLE ENCOUNTERS
----------------------
Level 1 - "Bandit Ambush":
[Bandit 3HP/3ATK][Bandit 3HP/3ATK][Leader 8HP/5ATK]

Level 3 - "Orc Warband":
      [Archer 4HP/4ATK][Archer 4HP/4ATK]
[Warrior 12HP/6ATK][Warrior 12HP/6ATK][Chieftain 20HP/8ATK]

Level 5 - "Undead Legion":
         [Necromancer 10HP/Summon][Necromancer 10HP/Summon]
[Skeleton 5HP/4ATK][Skeleton 5HP/4ATK][Skeleton 5HP/4ATK][Wight 15HP/7ATK]

